#: manual/filter-language.md:41
msgid "`key:( ... )` applies the key to every word and quoted text inside the brackets. `type:(food or medical)` is `type:food or type:medical`. Inside, the operators and brackets work as everywhere: `type:(food -junk)` is food that is not junk. A word inside is always a value, so `type:(stolen)` is the type called stolen; a key written inside keeps its own key: `type:(food or tag:x)`. To use `and`, `or` or `not` as a value, quote it: `type:(\"or\")`. Groups can nest."
msgstr ""

